Mechanism
main.rs App::drain retains latest Model Arc and command/focus/reply handling, marks scene_dirty; it performs no Scene::set_model.
The previous five production set_model call sites coalesce through one project_scene boundary.
main.rs App::redraw drains dirty data before consuming the tick as before. No-tick/occluded turns return without projecting.
gpu.rs splits the existing acquire code from draw. Unavailable/lost/size-mismatched targets retain their original result/reconfigure/error policy.
Only an acquired target permits project_scene; a refusal retains the pending marker and original redraw retry conditions.
Acquisition wait remains present-wait accounting, excluded from drain CPU wall phases.
headless.rs projects once in its existing dirty && submitted==rendered offscreen frame branch before layout/submit.
Scene projection / UiLayout / historical cell rendering use the same retained model in a frame. No protocol or pager change.
scene.rs adds only a cfg(test) per-instance projection counter. Production R5i counters remain in place.
R5i ModelApplied stamp now follows actual projection rather than mere Arc retention.

